# syncyard-power — scoped sudo for the Syncyard gatekeeper's
# Linux power signals (spec 042 FR-001; amendment 2026-11-17
# after field leg A).
#
# Why this exists: the gatekeeper's Linux power signal bodies
# run as the runner account inside linux.yml maintenance jobs.
# Field leg A (2026-11-17, tower-offsite) proved that an
# unprivileged `shutdown` from that account is refused by
# logind ("Interactive authentication required") — nothing is
# scheduled. The amended bodies therefore invoke ONLY through
# `sudo -n`, and this drop-in is the whole of the privilege
# they get:
#
#   sudo -n /usr/sbin/shutdown -r|-h +<minutes> "Syncyard gatekeeper power"
#   sudo -n /usr/sbin/shutdown -c                       (cancel)
#   sudo -n /usr/bin/systemctl reboot                   (immediate)
#   sudo -n /usr/bin/systemctl poweroff                 (immediate)
#
# /usr/sbin/shutdown is granted with any arguments (the
# bodies use exactly the forms above); the systemctl entries
# are pinned to the single argument each body uses. Nothing
# else is granted. Without this drop-in the signal body
# fails loudly by design — there is no unprivileged
# fallback.
#
# Install on each wave-1 Linux host BEFORE its first live
# power action:
#   1. Replace SYNCYARD_RUNNER_ACCOUNT below with the
#      account the host's linux.yml runner jobs run as.
#      On the tower-compute and tower-offsite lanes that
#      account is 'runner'; check per host — a host whose
#      runners were enrolled under another name needs its
#      own name here.
#   2. sudo install -o root -g root -m 0440 \
#        sudoers-syncyard-power /etc/sudoers.d/syncyard-power
#   3. sudo visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/syncyard-power
#      (must parse clean before the file is relied on)
#   4. Prove it AS the runner account, non-destructively:
#        sudo -n -l /usr/sbin/shutdown
#      must list the command. A password prompt or a
#      refusal means the drop-in is not in effect — do not
#      live-fire a power action on that host.
SYNCYARD_RUNNER_ACCOUNT ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/shutdown, /usr/bin/systemctl reboot, /usr/bin/systemctl poweroff
